{"id":"8e6e149b1b2e2a17dc13133c58b1e0707a310d8f60c9dab83c030d235b1a9f6b","pubkey":"101b30ee88c27a13de68bf7c8c06368ea3e3e837641595c18675677d18a46a45","created_at":1782563028,"content":"Lately, I've been trying to use AI to implement a libc-independent QUIC/HTTP3 protocol stack in C that runs entirely in user space\n\nIf this goes well, I'm thinking I could have it implement RFC 9220 too, and eventually build a Nostr relay running on WebSockets over QUIC\n\nSome might argue that it should be implemented in Rust or Zig. However, at present, C runs on virtually every compiler and architecture. Furthermore, I'm hoping it will allow us to pursue the ultimate in speed. You could say this is a proof of concept, or perhaps just a matter of personal ego\n\nIdeally, if possible, I would have liked to implement this myself rather than using AI, but that would likely take years\n\nhttps://github.com/Hakkadaikon/quic_vibe\n\n#grownostr","tags":[["r","https://github.com/Hakkadaikon/quic_vibe"],["t","grownostr"],["client","Damus"]]}
